# Contract Change Migration Guidance

When refactoring files that are part of this package's public contract, always provide a migration guide for downstream projects.

## Required when changing a contract

- State what contract changed (class/interface/DTO field/method/signature/behavior).
- Explain breaking impact for projects that consume this package.
- Provide concrete "before/after" usage examples.
- Provide a step-by-step fix checklist for consumer projects.
- Mention any temporary compatibility layer or deprecation path, if available.

If no consumer action is needed, explicitly write that the refactor is non-breaking and why.
